description
  Test: characters from outside plain ASCII.
  Curly "smart" quotes and en dashes get inserted when code is copied out
  of Word, Google Docs, or a chat app. They are not the characters our
  grammar uses, so the scanner should flag them. Accented letters are not
  letters in our grammar (only a-z and A-Z).
*/
import "scl.h"
implementations
function main return type integer is
variables
    define café of type real
begin
    display “Hello”
    set x = 5 – 2
    exit
endfun main

// EXPECT: Line 12: unknown character 'é'
// EXPECT: Line 14: unknown character '“'
// EXPECT: Line 14: unknown character '”'
// EXPECT: Line 15: unknown character '–'
